<title>UK: Gibbs Mew half year profits tumble.</title>
<headline>Gibbs Mew half year profits tumble.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>24 weeks ended September 14</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		7.83		   vs 14.21</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 4.0		    vs 4.0</p>
<p> Operating profit	 2.09		   vs 3.20</p>
<p> Pretax		     0.96		   vs 2.52</p>
<p> Turnover		   20.77		  vs 21.18</p>
<p>NOTE - Pub operator and brewer Gibbs Mew said results for the second half were expected to improve but would still be disappointing in comparison with last year. Its first half results reflected exceptional costs of 0.47 million stg for closing its Centric offices in April, launch costs of its new brands, lower sales volumes, the sale of pubs and continued investment in the free trade business.</p>
<p>Full company name - Gibbs Mew Plc</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
